<% page_title "Landing carousel" %>

<div id="c-admin-landing-settings">
  <div id="a-show">
    <h1>Landing carousel</h1>

    <p class="hint">
      The front page's first row. It draws from ONE board, newest first, and
      normally hides archive backfill -- an imported picture is new by post id
      even when it is years old, which is how a backfill run comes to drown the
      live captures the row exists to show.
    </p>

    <%= edit_form_for(@landing_setting, url: admin_landing_setting_path, method: :patch) do |f| %>
      <%= f.input :label, label: "Row heading", hint: "What visitors see above the row." %>
      <%= f.input :board, label: "Board", hint: "The bare slug, so 'b' for /b/ -- which is the DEGEN generals." %>
      <%= f.input :fresh_only, as: :boolean, label: "Freshly scraped only",
                  hint: "Hides anything the sampler tagged as archive-sourced." %>
      <%= f.submit "Save" %>
    <% end %>

    <h2>What that searches</h2>
    <p><code><%= @landing_setting.query %></code></p>
    <p class="hint">
      Two terms, which is the limit. A logged-out visitor may search two tags
      and the landing page runs as whoever is looking at it, so a third term
      would not narrow this row, it would empty it -- and an empty row is
      dropped from the page silently. That is why this is a set of choices
      rather than a box you type a search into.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>
